<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tiaret</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tahert</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tiaret is a city on the high plateaus of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. Nearby stood Tahert, founded in the 8th century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-ibn-rustam">Abd al-Rahman ibn Rustam</a> as the capital of the Ibadi Rustamid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">imamate</a>, a centre of trade and learning until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> destroyed it in 909. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djedars">Djedars</a>, royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> tombs of the 5th to 7th centuries, stand in the surrounding hills.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tiaret.jpg" alt="Tiaret" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tiarety14 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tiaret_at_night.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Abroad, they kept strained relations with the Ibadi Rustamids of <b>Tahert</b>, tense relations with the Zaydi Shi'ite Idrisids of Fez, and a hostile stance towards the Umayyads of Córdoba.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aghlabid-emirate">Aghlabid emirate · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Ibn Rustam fled west and later founded the Rustamid imamate at <b>Tahert</b>, carrying on the Ibadi state tradition.</blockquote><a href="/state/ibadi-imamate-of-tripolitania">Ibadi Imamate of Tripolitania</a></li><li><blockquote>After Roman and Vandal authority faded in the interior of Mauretania Caesariensis in the late 5th century, a Berber kingdom emerged in the Ouarsenis mountains and high plains around <b>Tiaret</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-the-ouarsenis">Kingdom of the Ouarsenis</a></li><li><blockquote>After its defeat in 761 he fled west and founded the city of <b>Tahert</b> (near modern Tiaret), where around 777 the Ibadi community elected him imam.</blockquote><a href="/state/rustamid-imamate">Rustamid imamate</a></li></ul></section>
